# Standards Terraform / Infrastructure as Code

## Principes fondamentaux

- **Idempotence** : safe to rerun, safe to fail, safe to rollback
- **Immutable** : remplacer plutôt que modifier
- **Versionné** : tout dans Git, revu, testé
- **State sacré** : toujours backup avant manipulation

## Workflow

```bash
terraform init      # Initialiser
terraform validate  # Valider syntaxe
terraform plan      # Prévisualiser changements
terraform apply     # Appliquer (après review du plan!)
```

**Règle d'or** : `plan` avant `apply`, toujours reviewer.

## Structure projet

```
terraform/
├── modules/                    # Modules réutilisables
│   ├── networking/
│   │   ├── main.tf
│   │   ├── variables.tf
│   │   ├── outputs.tf
│   │   └── README.md
│   └── compute/
├── environments/               # Par environnement
│   ├── dev/
│   │   ├── main.tf
│   │   ├── backend.tf
│   │   └── terraform.tfvars
│   ├── staging/
│   └── prod/
├── main.tf                     # Root module
├── variables.tf                # Déclaration variables
├── outputs.tf                  # Outputs exportés
├── providers.tf                # Configuration providers
├── versions.tf                 # Contraintes versions
└── locals.tf                   # Valeurs locales calculées
```

## Variables avec validation

```hcl
variable "environment" {
  type        = string
  description = "Deployment environment (dev, staging, prod)"

  validation {
    condition     = contains(["dev", "staging", "prod"], var.environment)
    error_message = "Environment must be dev, staging, or prod."
  }
}

variable "instance_count" {
  type        = number
  description = "Number of instances to create"
  default     = 1

  validation {
    condition     = var.instance_count >= 1 && var.instance_count <= 10
    error_message = "Instance count must be between 1 and 10."
  }
}

variable "allowed_cidrs" {
  type        = list(string)
  description = "List of CIDR blocks allowed to access the service"
  default     = []

  validation {
    condition = alltrue([
      for cidr in var.allowed_cidrs : can(cidrhost(cidr, 0))
    ])
    error_message = "All values must be valid CIDR blocks."
  }
}
```

## Locals pour valeurs calculées

```hcl
locals {
  # Tags communs à toutes les ressources
  common_tags = {
    Environment = var.environment
    Project     = var.project_name
    ManagedBy   = "terraform"
    Owner       = var.owner
    CostCenter  = var.cost_center
  }

  # Nom avec convention
  name_prefix = "${var.project_name}-${var.environment}"

  # Conditional logic
  is_production = var.environment == "prod"
  replica_count = local.is_production ? 3 : 1
}
```

## Ressources avec bonnes pratiques

```hcl
# ❌ MAUVAIS
resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  ami           = "ami-12345"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
}

# ✅ BON
resource "aws_instance" "application" {
  ami           = data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id
  instance_type = var.instance_type
  subnet_id     = var.subnet_id

  root_block_device {
    volume_size = var.root_volume_size
    encrypted   = true
  }

  metadata_options {
    http_tokens = "required"  # IMDSv2
  }

  tags = merge(local.common_tags, {
    Name = "${local.name_prefix}-app"
    Role = "application"
  })

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }
}
```

## Backend remote state

```hcl
# backend.tf
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = "company-terraform-state"
    key            = "project/env/terraform.tfstate"
    region         = "eu-west-1"
    encrypt        = true
    dynamodb_table = "terraform-locks"  # State locking
  }
}

# Ou Azure
terraform {
  backend "azurerm" {
    resource_group_name  = "terraform-state-rg"
    storage_account_name = "tfstate12345"
    container_name       = "tfstate"
    key                  = "project/env/terraform.tfstate"
  }
}
```

## Versions et providers

```hcl
# versions.tf
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.5.0"

  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
    random = {
      source  = "hashicorp/random"
      version = "~> 3.5"
    }
  }
}
```

## Outputs explicites

```hcl
output "instance_id" {
  description = "ID of the EC2 instance"
  value       = aws_instance.application.id
}

output "instance_public_ip" {
  description = "Public IP address of the instance"
  value       = aws_instance.application.public_ip
}

output "connection_string" {
  description = "Connection string for the database"
  value       = "postgresql://${var.db_user}@${aws_db_instance.main.endpoint}/${var.db_name}"
  sensitive   = true
}
```

## Sécurité - Secrets

```hcl
# ❌ INTERDIT - secrets dans le code
resource "aws_db_instance" "db" {
  password = "mysecretpassword"
}

# ✅ BON - depuis Secrets Manager
data "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "db" {
  secret_id = "prod/db/password"
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "db" {
  password = data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db.secret_string
}

# ✅ BON - variable sensitive
variable "db_password" {
  type        = string
  description = "Database password"
  sensitive   = true
}
```

## Module réutilisable

```hcl
# modules/vpc/main.tf
resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block           = var.cidr_block
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
  enable_dns_support   = true

  tags = merge(var.tags, {
    Name = var.name
  })
}

# modules/vpc/variables.tf
variable "name" {
  type        = string
  description = "Name of the VPC"
}

variable "cidr_block" {
  type        = string
  description = "CIDR block for the VPC"

  validation {
    condition     = can(cidrhost(var.cidr_block, 0))
    error_message = "Must be a valid CIDR block."
  }
}

variable "tags" {
  type        = map(string)
  description = "Tags to apply to resources"
  default     = {}
}

# modules/vpc/outputs.tf
output "vpc_id" {
  description = "ID of the created VPC"
  value       = aws_vpc.main.id
}
```

## Checklist Terraform

- [ ] Variables avec description et validation
- [ ] Locals pour tags communs et valeurs calculées
- [ ] Backend remote avec state locking
- [ ] Versions terraform et providers fixées
- [ ] Outputs documentés avec sensitive si nécessaire
- [ ] Pas de secrets dans le code
- [ ] Tags sur toutes les ressources
- [ ] README dans chaque module
- [ ] `terraform fmt` avant commit
- [ ] `terraform validate` en CI
